The plan calls the gate repo getai/factory-gates. On getai.ghe.com the
gate and the held-out tests live in the central org, GetAI-IP (decided
3 November 2026). Set GATE_REPO, the owner of all six App token steps
(each reads only factory-gates or factory-holdout), the holdout checkout
and the header comment to it, and the GATE_REPO assertion in
tests/test_workflow.py.

README: no longer a staging copy; names the central org, the four orgs
that will use the gate, and the caller design as a later slice. The move
steps now name GetAI-IP.

rulesets/org.json and templates/CODEOWNERS are unchanged: they describe
an org that uses the gate (AI-Business-Solutions) and are hashed.
None of the changed files is hashed, so scripts.sha256 is unchanged.

141 tests OK, manifest verify clean, rulesets check clean.

